  "version": "0.2.3",
  "comment": "Deterministic, ordered rule table. First rule whose conditions all match any tool in a turn wins. Regexes are matched against the concatenated tool name, agent subagent_type, command, path and (optionally) result text. No project names are hard-coded: only generic workflow artifacts, tool names and command/path signatures. v0.2.1 adds structural rules for plan-mode control transitions, human-in-the-loop clarification, agent subagent_type, monitor_command build/test jobs, harness self-tests and result/report artifacts. v0.2.2 adds plan_review / agent_output control tools and the verification harness tree (*.py, *.sh, contracts/tests/examples/fixtures, README) so the promotion's harness-authoring wall is no longer UNKNOWN. v0.2.3 adds the Verification Layer runner execution signature (run_verification.sh / verification/runner / orchestrator.py) -> T7 so running the harness is never UNKNOWN.",
